ngs. A plain\\n   120\\t   persistent set — structural equality is context identity. Well-founded:\\n   121\\t   env values were created before the env that holds them, so the\\n   122\\t   env-reachable graph is acyclic; cycles arise only through the store,\\n   123\\t   which is no part of any context.\\\"\\n   124\\t  [env E]\\n   125\\t  (into #{} (mapcat #(abstract-value env %)) (vals E)))\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   129\\t;; §5.1 code-facts(address)\\n   130\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   131\\t\\n   132\\t(defn- closure-ranges\\n   133\\t  \\\"`[[c body r] …]` for every `:closure` of canonical vector `v`: the body\\n   134\\t   of the closure at pc `c` is `[body, r]`, `r` the first `:return` at or\\n   135\\t   after `body` (§5.1.1). nil `r` when there is none.\\\"\\n   136\\t  [v]\\n   137\\t  (let [n (count v)]\\n   138\\t    (keep (fn [c]\\n   139\\t            (let [t (nth v c)]\\n   140\\t              (when (= :closure (nth t 0))\\n   141\\t                (let [body (nth t 2)]\\n   142\\t                  [c body (first (filter #(= :return (nth (nth v %) 0))\\n   143\\t                                         (range body n)))]))))\\n   144\\t          (range n))))\\n   145\\t\\n   146\\t\\n   147\\t(defn- layout-conforms?\\n   148\\t  \\\"Whether `v` has the `\\\\\\\"ast-to-bytecode\\\\\\\"` body layout the range rule\\n   149\\t   reads: every body closed by a `:return`, no body covering pc 0 (bodies\\n   150\\t   follow the main code), and bodies pairwise disjoint (contiguous, never\\n   151\\t   interleaved). A vector that fails is ruled all-free (§5.1.1).\\\"\\n   152\\t  [v]\\n   153\\t  (let [ranges (closure-ranges v)\\n   154\\t        spans (distinct (map (fn [[_ b r]] [b r]) ranges))]\\n   155\\t    (and (every? (fn [[b r]] (and r (pos? b))) spans)\\n   156\\t         (= (count spans) (count (dis