mages, else from the caller's `fetch` (e.g. over\\n   299\\t   `yin.vm.content/fetch-vector` / `load-rows`). A caller fetch that throws\\n   300\\t   the content namespace's \\\\\\\"resolves to no payload\\\\\\\" is a miss, as nil is.\\\"\\n   301\\t  [vm fetch]\\n   302\\t  (fn [address]\\n   303\\t    (or (some-> (get (:code-aliases vm) address)\\n   304\\t                (->> (get (:code vm)))\\n   305\\t                image->vector)\\n   306\\t        (when fetch\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_36\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The review is now at a request-changes threshold independent of the pending lanes: Section 4.1’s scanner contract is not implemented, and the new byte-count code lacks the Dart type alias. The worklist also permits unbounded default traversal and checks its byte cap only after decode. I’m preparing line-specific fixes; I did not rerun tests.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_37\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '247,324p;390,485p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_37\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '247,324p;390,485p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   247\\t\\n   248\\t### 4.1 The format record\\n   249\\t\\n   250\\tA format record is a plain map held in linker-local state. B6 fixed three\\n   251\\tfunction slots; this revision replaces one, renames one, and adds four:\\n   252\\t\\n   253\\t```clojure\\n   254\\t{:format              :yin.debruijn.code      ; the dispatch key\\n   255\\t :contract            \\\"b1\\\"                    ; contract revision name\\n   256\\t :identity-fn         (fn [value] identity)   ; mint: publish! only\\n   257\\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [identity value] boolean) ; step 3\\n   258\\t :row-defect-fn       (fn [value] defect-or-nil)    ; step 2, per part\\n   259\\t :validate-fn         (fn [value] defect-or-nil)    ; step 4, whole\\n   260\\t :obligations-fn      (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\\n   261\\t :definitions-fn      (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\\n   262\\t :applications-fn     (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\\n   263\\t :parts-fn            (fn [value] [address ...])}   ; step 2 worklist\\n   264\\t```\\n   265\\t\\n   266\\t- `:identity-fn` mints an identity from a payload. It is used by\\n   267\\t  `publish!` and never by verification.\\n   268\\t- `:identity-matches-fn` is the step-3 check, directed by the identity.\\n   269\\t  For H and R it is `(= identity (image-hash value))`, a contract-pinned\\n   270\\t  hash with one algorithm. For the storage-derived formats it is\\n   271\\t  `(jing/segment-matches? identity value)`, so a value minted under\\n   272\\t  `:sha256` while the default is `:blake3` verifies under the algorithm\\n   273\\t  the identity names and never fails spuriously.\\n   274\\t- `:row-defect-fn` validates one fetched part on its own, before any\\n   275\\t  address it references is enqueued: tag, arity, slot kinds, saturation.\\n   276\\t  For single-payload formats it is the whole validator, run early.\\n   277\\t- `:parts-fn` returns the storage addresses a fetched payload references\\n   278\\t  and without which it is incomplete. For the three single-payload\\n   279\\t  formats it returns nothing. For `:yin.ast/code` it returns the child\\n   280\\t  row ids of a row body.\\n   281\\t- `:obligations-fn`, `:definitions-fn`, and `:applications-fn` are\\n   282\\t  **position-bearing scanners** with one shared result shape:\\n   283\\t\\n   284\\t  ```clojure\\n   285\\t  ;; :obligations-fn  value -> [{:name sym :at position :in-body? b}]\\n   286\\t  ;; :definitions-fn  value -> [{:name sym :at position\\n   287\\t  ;;                             :conditional? b}]\\n   288\\t  ;; :applications-fn value -> [{:at position}]\\n   289\\t  ;; position: a tree occurrence path [root-address path] for\\n   290\\t  ;;           :yin.ast/code; a pc for the vector formats\\n   291\\t  ```\\n   292\\t\\n   293\\t  `:conditional?` is true when any `:if` branch, jump target range, or\\n   294\\t  lambda body encloses the definition; `:in-body?` is true when a\\n   295\\t  lambda body encloses the occurrence; an `:applications-fn` record is\\n   296\\t  one **application site**: a position at which this image may apply a\\n   297\\t  closure it creates -- a direct call site, a call of an imported\\n   298\\t  name, or a call of a primitive that receives a function argument,\\n   299\\t  because the callee may apply what it is handed. Dominance between\\n   300\\t  two positions is decided by the linker from these fields and the\\n   301\\t  format's order (step 5a). For the AST record all three scanners are\\n   302\\t  Datalog over the rows: `yin.vm/free-names` today returns a symbol\\n   303\\t  set, and is extended (or wrapped by an occurrence-scoped query over\\n   304\\t  the same rules) to return each occurrence's path; the definitions\\n   305\\t  scanner is the store-key query behind `yin.vm/ast-requirements`\\n   306\\t  with the binding row's path and its enclosing tags; the application\\n   307\\t  scanner is the application-row query over the same relation. For\\n   308\\t  the vector formats all three are operand scans by pc (`:var`\\n   309\\t  against `:store-put`, `:load-free` against the `yin/def` call\\n   310\\t  sites, the call opcodes for applications) with conditional target\\n   311\\t  ranges taken from the `:jump-if` and body operands. A format whose\\n   312\\t  scanner returns positions as `nil` is admitted and falls under the\\n   313\\t  conservative degradation of step 5a: every occurrence is retained\\n   314\\t  as an obligation, and with no application positions no occurrence\\n   315\\t  inside a lambda body is discharged at all.\\n   316\\t\\n   317\\t`fetch` and `step` contain no branch on `:format`. Adding a fifth backend\\n   318\\tis one more record.\\n   319\\t\\n   320\\t### 4.2 The six steps\\n   321\\t\\n   322\\tThe order is B6's, unchanged, and remains load-bearing for the reasons\\n   323\\tB6 gives. An admission check precedes step 1; step 2 is a bounded\\n   324\\tworklist; steps 1 and 2 are stream exchanges (section 6); step 5 has a\\n   390\\t   The result of step 2 is the root value plus, for a multi-part\\n   391\\t   format, the map of every fetched part by address.\\n   392\\t3. **Verify format identity.** `(:identity-matches-fn format)` over the\\n   393\\t   requested identity and the root value. For H and R this is a\\n   394\\t   different hash under a different preimage from step 2 and catches a\\n   395\\t   stale or swapped index entry, a descriptor disagreement, or a\\n   396\\t   contract version disagreement (all `:hash-mismatch`, as in B6). For\\n   397\\t   the storage-derived formats it is `segment-matches?` under the\\n   398\\t   identity's own algorithm; it still runs, because it is the only check\\n   399\\t   that the *index* did not point the identity at a different, correctly\\n   400\\t   stored payload.\\n   401\\t4. **Validate structural and liveness invariants.** The format's\\n   402\\t   validator runs over the complete value: for a tree, over the\\n   403\\t   assembled row set (`:id-resolves`, `:acyclic`, `:root-reachable` are\\n   404\\t   whole-tree rules that step 2's row-local check cannot run); for a\\n   405\\t   vector, over the vector; for a register image, including the\\n   406\\t   ascending, bounded, exact live-set rules. A validator that throws is\\n   407\\t   `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:validator-refused`.\\n   408\\t5. **Verify dependency closure.** Two halves.\\n   409\\t   - *5a, at the linker: obligations.* Two scans run over the verified\\n   410\\t     value. `:obligations-fn` yields the free-name occurrences, each\\n   411\\t     with its position: for a tree, the occurrence path and whether it\\n   412\\t     lies inside a `:lambda` body; for a vector, the pc and whether it\\n   413\\t     lies in a body rather than the main sequence. `:definitions-fn`\\n   414\\t     yields the **definition set** with positions: every constant store\\n   415\\t     key the image binds at module level (the section 7.7 store-key\\n   416\\t     query of `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`: `:vm/store-put` rows,\\n   417\\t     `:store-put` operands, `yin/def` applications with a constant key),\\n   418\\t     each with the position of the binding in the main sequence.\\n   419\\t     A definition discharges an occurrence by **defined-before-use\\n   420\\t     under control-flow dominance**, not by subtraction of names and\\n   421\\t     not by source order alone. Source order says a definition is\\n   422\\t     written earlier; dominance says it has executed by the time the\\n   423\\t     occurrence runs. Only the second discharges, and where dominance\\n   424\\t     cannot be established the obligation is **retained**, never\\n   425\\t     dropped:\\n   426\\t     - A definition is *unconditional* when it sits in the main\\n   427\\t       sequence at top level or inside a `:do` (for a tree) or at a pc\\n   428\\t       in the main sequence outside every conditional target range\\n   429\\t       (for a vector); it is *conditional* when any `:if` branch, any\\n   430\\t       jump target, or any lambda body encloses it. A conditional\\n   431\\t       definition discharges nothing statically: the linker cannot know\\n   432\\t       the branch was taken, so an occurrence that depends on it keeps\\n   433\\t       its obligation and is checked at the receiver under 5b exactly\\n   434\\t       as an undefined name would be, and the manifest must declare it\\n   435\\t       or the link is `:undeclared-free`. This is conservative by\\n   436\\t       design: a module that defines a name only in one branch and\\n   437\\t       reads it afterwards must declare what the name means when the\\n   438\\t       branch is not taken.\\n   439\\t     - An occurrence in the main sequence (outside every lambda body)\\n   440\\t       is discharged only by an unconditional definition of that name\\n   441\\t       that dominates it: for a tree, an earlier sibling in the same\\n   442\\t       or an enclosing top-level `:do`; for a vector, an earlier pc in\\n   443\\t       the main sequence with no conditional target range between the\\n   444\\t       two. A main-sequence occurrence whose only definitions are all\\n   445\\t       later or all conditional and later is `:use-before-definition`:\\n   446\\t       in the isolated store it would read nothing, and no manifest\\n   447\\t       declaration may stand in for a name the module itself defines\\n   448\\t       unconditionally later. An occurrence whose only definitions are\\n   449\\t       conditional and earlier retains its obligation, per the rule\\n   450\\t       above.\\n   451\\t     - An occurrence inside a lambda body is discharged only by an\\n   452\\t       unconditional definition of that name that is **proven to\\n   453\\t       execute before every application of the enclosing closure**.\\n   454\\t       The body runs at application time, and the applications the\\n   455\\t       image performs are exactly its application sites\\n   456\\t       (`:applications-fn`, section 4.1). No value-flow analysis\\n   457\\t       bounds which closures a site can apply, so every site is\\n   458\\t       treated as a possible application of every closure the image\\n   459\\t       creates: a definition discharges a body occurrence only when\\n   460\\t       it dominates every application site in the main sequence,\\n   461\\t       under the same order rules as a main-sequence occurrence. A\\n   462\\t       site inside another body needs no separate case: it executes\\n   463\\t       only after some main-sequence site has executed, which the\\n   464\\t       definition dominates, or after halt, by which an unconditional\\n   465\\t       definition has executed. An image with no application site\\n   466\\t       discharges a body occurrence against every unconditional\\n   467\\t       definition of the name: nothing applies the closure before\\n   468\\t       halt, and after halt the read runs against the module store\\n   469\\t       the relocation carries (section 7.3), never the receiver's\\n   470\\t       ambient bindings. Where any site is not dominated, the\\n   471\\t       obligation is **retained** and must be declared by the\\n   472\\t       manifest exactly as a conditional definition's must. Revision\\n   473\\t       r5 discharged a body occurrence against any later\\n   474\\t       unconditional definition and left an early application to\\n   475\\t       \\\"fail in the child at run time\\\"; the second half was wrong:\\n   476\\t       the read does not reliably error, because `resolve-var`\\n   477\\t       (`yin.vm.engine`) falls through to primitives and the module\\n   478\\t       registry and may bind an ambient name whose profile was never\\n   479\\t       checked. r6 withdraws the claim and retains the obligation.\\n   480\\t     Where a scanner cannot compute positions at all, the rule\\n   481\\t     degrades to the conservative side: every occurrence keeps its\\n   482\\t     obligation and no definition discharges anything. Under that\\n   483\\t     degradation a self-defining module still links only if its\\n   484\\t     manifest declares every name it reads, which is more obligation\\n   485\\t     than necessary and never less.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_38\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-25 07:17:54 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-25 14:17:54 ICT\\n\\nP1 | [linker.cljc:241](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:241) | All four records return name collections as `:obligations-fn` and omit `:definitions-fn` and `:applications-fn`; fetch passes those names directly to receiver discharge ([line 580](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:580)). This cannot perform the position-bearing, defined-before-use and conditional/lambda analysis required by [Section 4.1](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:260). | Add the three position-bearing scanners and tests for dominance, early application, and conditional definitions; adapt step 5 to consume their records.\\n\\nP1 | [linker.cljc:393](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:393) | The ClojureDart branch uses `typed/Uint8List`, but the namespace has no `dart:typed_data` alias ([imports](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:22)). | Add the conditional Dart import or use a type already imported, then confirm the Dart lane is green.\\n\\nP1 | [linker.cljc:525](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:525) | All bounds default to nil, so the ordinary fetch path has no finite worklist limit. Even when supplied, `:max-bytes` is checked after fetch and decode, and child addresses are enqueued before a parts-limit check ([worklist](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:489)). An untrusted large row can consume unbounded decode or queue memory before refusal. | Require finite composition bounds (or safe defaults) for every fetch path; check byte size before decode and enforce the parts budget while enqueuing.\\n\\nThe four-file scope, identity-directed matching, retired-loader caller migration, and edited-line hygiene check out. The stale [completion.cljc docstring](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/completion.cljc:296) is deferred, non-blocking debt outside the file box. I did not rerun suites; the supplied JVM run is green, while Node and Dart results remain pending.\\n\\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\\nSign-off: DENIED\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":19966719,\"cached_input_tokens\":18762624,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":92960,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":54780}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
